{"step_index":1506,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-12T01:52:35Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-12T09:52:35+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-12T09:52:50+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-12T09:52:35+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-12T09:52:50+08:00\nThe search for \"SQLite FTS5 INSERT OR REPLACE DELETE transaction concurrency busy_timeout WAL mode Windows\" returned the following summary:\nWhen combining **SQLite FTS5**, heavy concurrent writing (`INSERT OR REPLACE`, `DELETE`), **WAL mode**, and **Windows file-locking semantics**, developers frequently hit `SQLITE_BUSY` (\"database is locked\") errors[1][2]. \n\nFTS5 tables are complex virtual tables[3] that internally maintain multiple index b-trees (terms, postings, columns). An `INSERT OR REPLACE` (which translates to a `DELETE` followed by an `INSERT`) or an explicit `DELETE` causes intense write amplification. Under high concurrency, this triggers lock contention[4].\n\nThe following architectural blueprint addresses these specific failure modes on Windows.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Issues on Windows & FTS5\n* **Windows File Locking (POSIX vs. Win32):** Unlike Linux, Windows enforces strict file-lock semantics via the Win32 API. If a reader or checkpoint operation has a lock handle open, or if multiple handles fight over the `-wal` / `-shm` files, Windows bubbles up sharing violations more aggressively as `SQLITE_BUSY`.\n* **Deferred Transaction Upgrades (The Silent Deadlock):** If multiple threads/connections start a transaction with a plain `BEGIN` (which is *deferred*), they acquire a read lock. When they subsequently try to execute an `INSERT`/`DELETE`, they attempt to escalate to a write lock simultaneously. If two connections try to upgrade at the same time, one gets blocked and a deadlock or immediate timeout occurs[5].\n* **FTS5 Write Weight:** FTS5 updates write to multiple internal segments. Long transactions keep write locks active longer, starving other threads[2].\n\n---\n\n### 2. The Solution Checklist\n\n#### A. Order Your PRAGMAs Correctly (Crucial for Cold Starts)\nIf you configure your database upon opening, ensure `busy_timeout` is set **before** `journa\n<truncated 3351 bytes>\nnjFe8ConOmV_twxCLxOd7r-5I5lcTrYhtlaF8lFdFH)\n[2] [dbpro.app](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFWVNX1dKfaRnO6SMVNaRJN0JoyxY7uOBekMA5ocbEvDVP0tOcrMGNI8hz0pdRbOhyaQHGzeyWPqmBuWhOqntoGyIzXqoQXECVoy_6NuL9MADPxXhRrn5vM6K4J_aVMLRa-6IgpeLPl74ifFukzxdM=)\n[3] [sqlite.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGFiK9jOP7hDrvPo_UoqSixcGflhnmZPRJVVZUUpTJW7Tj9QWBeuPepX_u6HTxtegUWBSzW3YREzrE8Q_CniBuOpqJToUq3atSO0WfVvK9otpqH)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEhZvid5k8dOSAIC3DX2C-3Eqb05wNIbem3W3s0EA5Fe48Rj-yZBpxxDgiP8veXQKnSXkde9I8ung5wqM5t2RYnMA70GGiJOBknw10HRp299pXrnlM5cjnyV6sl__a1N4o5nEIUVQ==)\n[5] [berthub.eu](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHGZd5sAXttRryEroaVBEk1-7jGw382-fxwDzYYmpTU91zVdpLA2ZPopAgAs6_9iYmumY9h-y-cCxTUIE-QA5qJLJhxjI1Hsj1BM_ObuG8XuxVbDa2G3ca3Iwinmv4Bn6IN9A8rKQ2vbGcw6xZwFdMvM4zjOZy9GXYzokRKMvADQbqTeMCtUYbRhJ3_zxzpJBM=)\n[6] [cursor.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFa6Kp5YN7SgyVLwzf_QrnVfycmqKGAnt8Q102wk96LAixnNmWsixZJ5PN1HGvSqffgFkA2VfG4Y10-qQ60E5YrytRuQHRYHMDrbBouIoUIQJSIKK1YR-TubfzuAmFe-eZ169XsL9OO9KlM9Ng0OBc6iuT02vQTc8h79I1aKSYG_gajVTrfR3Kxe6zQlQkcpNVgax0eUJoSSe-heQ4GSymzpXUMu6cdzSbvVIiDA4iZqXN-9VFsEQkKQImPCjP26zhVuVImajg80KlJHaxWbjtT8voXP1p_ErF59kCB1AoGkYGnz2ANpu_v)\n[7] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFzrJpcij1rgcKhZonBklMy1SIGeoCAUGwR_dQ8zEstkhKbX1Ou-mKfUYFd9DqOxkU7PDoTyGkbxWvWoPaEWW73LM3Q6S2FtCLzjZyKnPA2gGV6fOzdxHTr0kkWRMlJsRvkHvQqB7s_zF0NKAFDePQnX-nXj6xL-HqG8qp_6YDs0rfSn_-mQ-4Xsq677zO6QDBds_nZwuE=)\n[8] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGNsAv94X